  "definition": "An identity binding is a member of an agent's identity set that ties one identity to the key management arrangement behind it. In the SAC-CG Agent Ontology it is the class `IdentityBinding`, declared without a definition; this one follows from its properties.[^1] An `IdentitySet` reaches it through the `identity` property, and its declared property `keyManagementSystem` is a datatype property with a string value. The value names the [[Key Management System]] that holds the keys for the identity.",
